1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,830
Meet Wave Protocol.

2
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:03,536
Token baskets, in balance.

3
00:00:03,536 --> 00:00:06,522
One token brings your basket into view.

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:15,801
Managing a portfolio means many swaps, constant rebalancing, and exposing reads to an RPC provider.

5
00:00:15,801 --> 00:00:23,718
Wave brings a basket into one token, with fair value, target allocation, and private visibility in the same journey.

6
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:27,615
Growth is the existing flagship.

7
00:00:27,615 --> 00:00:32,157
Assets, target weights, fees, and net asset value come from contracts.

8
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:35,048
This button prepares one hundred test USDC.

9
00:00:35,048 --> 00:00:40,416
Approval and the mock token faucet are verified; the deposit is still pending.

10
00:00:40,416 --> 00:00:42,894
No completed deposit is staged here.

11
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,392
Uniswap v4 executes the swaps.

12
00:00:47,392 --> 00:00:53,656
Nav Guard Hook compares the approved pool price with Chainlink based net asset value before each swap.

13
00:00:53,656 --> 00:01:01,393
Outside a one percent band, a trade toward NAV pays zero point zero five percent; a trade away pays one percent.

14
00:01:01,393 --> 00:01:05,077
Inside the band, both pay zero point zero five percent.

15
00:01:05,077 --> 00:01:07,656
Live directional swap receipts are still pending.

16
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:12,812
Chainlink feeds value the holdings.

17
00:01:12,812 --> 00:01:20,052
CRE proposes a bounded rebalance, while the vault independently enforces weight, turnover, timing, and execution limits.

18
00:01:20,052 --> 00:01:22,315
A genuine hold is acceptable.

19
00:01:22,315 --> 00:01:27,745
The workflow compiles, but real CRE broadcast and receiver proof remain pending.

20
00:01:27,745 --> 00:01:30,912
Local reports do not replace that proof.

21
00:01:33,550 --> 00:01:37,969
Withdraw into mock USDC, or take the underlying assets in kind.

22
00:01:37,969 --> 00:01:39,977
Healthy feeds crystallize creator fees.

23
00:01:39,977 --> 00:01:46,807
Stale feed in kind exits stay immediate and pro rata after the withdrawal fee, with no reserve.

24
00:01:46,807 --> 00:01:49,217
They can avoid uncrystallized creator fees.

25
00:01:49,217 --> 00:01:51,627
These are controls, not completed withdrawals.

26
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:56,882
Anon RPC is the default for application reads.

27
00:01:56,882 --> 00:02:00,630
This short session shows actual startup and method counters.

28
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:05,211
Stopping the private worker rejects a read without increasing direct successes.

29
00:02:05,211 --> 00:02:08,542
It is partial evidence, not full lifecycle acceptance.

30
00:02:08,542 --> 00:02:11,041
Wallet RPC and bootstrap are separate.

31
00:02:11,041 --> 00:02:13,123
On chain holdings remain public.

32
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:27,517
The public record verifies forty two deployment transactions, plus approval and the mock token faucet, using PublicNode and Tenderly.

33
00:02:27,517 --> 00:02:30,821
Provider diversity does not prove independent infrastructure.

34
00:02:30,821 --> 00:02:33,181
Sixty eight local tests pass.

35
00:02:33,181 --> 00:02:38,373
Missing live deposits, swaps, withdrawals, and CRE execution stay visibly pending.

36
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:44,625
Wave Protocol.

37
00:02:44,625 --> 00:02:46,775
Token baskets, in balance.

38
00:02:46,775 --> 00:02:48,387
Uniswap for execution.

39
00:02:48,387 --> 00:02:51,612
Chainlink for valuation and bounded allocation.

40
00:02:51,612 --> 00:02:54,837
Anon RPC for less RPC exposure.

41
00:02:54,837 --> 00:02:58,599
Unaudited Sepolia, mock assets, no promised returns.
